# (The recorded baselines under benchmarks/baselines/ ARE tracked — see benchmarks/README.md.)
preflight-receipt.json
target/bench-run/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python

# Local Python virtualenv for the dev-time wylde_check linter (.venv is not tracked).
# NOTE: uv.lock was deleted in the full-Rust cutover (commit 2f5aa82) and is no
# longer committed — there is no runtime Python dependency lockfile anymore.
.venv/

# Test / lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Engineering record (slice reports). Canonical tracked home is the private
# PeopleWonder/wylde-planning repo, junctioned in at Core/outputs (see
# docs/branch-and-release-policy.md "Where things live"). Ignored wholesale here
# so the junction is invisible to this public repo.
outputs/

# gpui GUI build output (the Tauri+Svelte tree was deleted at the
# slice-11 cutover; the standalone Core/GUI/ Cargo workspace builds here)
Core/GUI/target/

# Cargo build artifacts (backend Rust workspace at rust/)
rust/target/

# Installer build output (tools/installer/build-installer.ps1 stages here)
release-artifacts/

# Any other Cargo target dirs (catch-all)
target/

# Out-of-tree runtime buckets (container-of-repos). Core's tracked tree
# stays just-Core: the three buckets ship EMPTY and are populated
# out-of-band, each item keeping its own independent .git. The lifecycle
# registry + extension bridge discover whatever is dropped in at runtime,
# and the boot/shutdown paths cleanly no-op when a bucket is absent or
# empty ("core works without"). See outputs/wylde-out-of-tree-runtime-plan.md.
#   * Services/      — sibling full-tier service repos (lifecycle-supervised)
#   * Extensions/    — leave-the-ecosystem extensions (extension-bridge)
#   * Core/Plugins/  — compiled-in plugin crates (opt-in; wired into the
#                      rust/ workspace by hand when present — see
#                      rust/crates/wylde-harness/src/plugins/mod.rs)
/Services/
/Extensions/
/Core/Plugins/

# Local data (runtime state — never committed)
data/
logs/
*.log
.wylde/

# Runtime service registry (regenerated by discovery on boot). Seed lives at services.yaml.seed.
Core/Network/services.yaml

# Per-test scratch dir (conftest redirects the IPC audit log here). Runtime
# artifact — was tracked by mistake; dirties the tree on every test run.
Core/shared/tests/_tmp/

# Editors / IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/

# Environment variables / secrets — never committed
# (.env.example / .env.sample stay tracked as templates)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.local.env
secrets.yaml
secrets.toml
secrets.json
*.secret
*.secret.*

Core/Memgraph/vendor/

# ─── PLANNING DOCS: PRIVATE, *NOT* UNTRACKED — read this before assuming ───
#
# `docs/plans/` is a **DIRECTORY JUNCTION** into a separate private repo:
#     C:\Users\aaron\Wylde\Core\docs\plans  ->  C:\Users\aaron\Wylde\wylde-planning\plans
#
# Ignoring it HERE is the mechanism that keeps internal strategy out of THIS
# public repo. It does **not** mean the content is untracked, local-only, or
# disposable. It is version-controlled — in `PeopleWonder/wylde-planning`
# (private), not in `wylde`.
#
# ⚠️ Edits you make under `docs/plans/` land in wylde-planning's WORKING TREE.
#    They are real and they are NOT committed by anything in this repo:
#        cd ../wylde-planning && git status && git add -A && git commit && git push
#    `git status` here will never mention them. That repo has its own CI
#    (`plans-check.yml`): frontmatter/lifecycle validity, and `INDEX.md` must be
#    REGENERATED (`tools/gen_index.py`), never hand-edited. Bump `last_reviewed`
#    when you revise a plan.
#
# This comment used to read "Local-only planning docs (kept on disk for
# reference, not published)". That predated wylde-planning and the junction, and
# it was read — reasonably — as "not version-controlled anywhere", which caused
# real roadmap edits to be dismissed as worthless scratch. The line was false;
# it is now the signpost. Keep it accurate if the arrangement changes.
docs/plans/

# Private planning/design docs — STILL genuinely local-only, unlike docs/plans/
# above. These are NOT in wylde-planning and NOT tracked anywhere: they exist on
# one disk, with no backup. That is the same durability gap the planning repo was
# created to close for docs/plans/, and these never got moved into it.
#
# Three of them have now BEEN moved (2026-07-16, maintainer's call) and their
# entries are gone from this list — `privacy-plan.md` (active),
# `wylde-android-app-plan.md` (deferred) and `wylde-rust-migration-master-plan.md`
# (retired `legacy`: the full-Rust cutover it plans already happened) now live in
# wylde-planning and are reachable at `docs/plans/` through the junction. The
# rest below are still one-disk; moving any of them is the maintainer's call.
